Phase 29 — break test for session-close's narrative check
=========================================================

Taken in the chat session's own sandbox, 2026-08-12, on the commit that adds the
check (dfc9a5d + this script). `bash scripts/break-narrative-phase.sh`, run
twice: the first run is below the second, because it found a defect in the
HARNESS and that is worth keeping.

WHAT IS BEING MEASURED. session-close.sh sets one global `fail`, and two of its
checks - a clean working tree and HEAD == origin/main - cannot pass in a sandbox
that is mid-session by construction. The script's exit status is therefore
confounded here and is NOT the reading; the reading is the narrative section's
own lines. `make -s gates` is stubbed by a shim on PATH: different section of
the script, slow, and several of its gates need a browser. The unconfounded run
is `make session-close` on the devbox at the end of this session, and it can
only ever show the control - which is exactly why this file exists.

THE DEFECT IS REPRODUCED, NOT SIMULATED. Variant [B] puts the repository back
into the state main was actually in on 2026-08-11: Phase 27's block on top,
Phase 28 closed, both dated the same day.

